CM 1MHz_tower's LD set exactly as the corpus deck writes it (momwire#415):
CM one card per leg, tags 3, 6, 9 and 12, under a live GR cell.  Tags 6, 9
CM and 12 are OUTSIDE the cell, so NEC drops all three in silence -- and then
CM replicates tag 3's load onto them anyway, which is why the oracle's answer
CM for this deck is 1MHz_tower.deck's to every printed digit.  momwire
CM refuses it by name instead: a card discarded without a diagnostic is a
CM defect worth naming, and the deck's author cannot tell from the printout
CM which of the two rules produced the number.
